                            <comment id="15228251" author="iveselovskiy" created="Wed, 6 Apr 2016 13:37:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/609&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/609&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
added test org.apache.ignite.internal.processors.hadoop.HadoopNoHadoopMapReduceTest .&lt;br/&gt;
tests are passing on TC.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15234827" author="vozerov" created="Mon, 11 Apr 2016 10:06:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ivan, we need to improve the fix:&lt;br/&gt;
1) The same exception should be thrown if any &lt;tt&gt;HadoopNoopProcessor&lt;/tt&gt; method is called. For now some methods throw &lt;tt&gt;IllegalStateException&lt;/tt&gt;, some throw &lt;tt&gt;IgniteCheckedException&lt;/tt&gt;, other methods return &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;false&lt;/tt&gt;. This is inconsistent. &lt;br/&gt;
2) Let&apos;s improve error message. It should be something like &quot;Hadoop module is not loaded (please ensure that ignite-hadoop.jar is in classpath).&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15235505" author="iveselovskiy" created="Mon, 11 Apr 2016 17:12:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;fixed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
